  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Corner choice – shoot or pass, three options in front of goal",
  "description": "Half the court, goalkeeper in goal. Three lines on the same side: A with the balls a little in from the boards near the centre line, B on the boards halfway down and C in the corner next to the goal. A passes to B and heads straight for the slot. B plays the ball down to C in the corner and carries on to the far post. C passes out to A in front of goal, who plays it straight back.\n\nNow C chooses: shoot, pass to B at the far post or play it back to A. Whoever does not finish follows up for the rebound. Rotate A to B, B to C and C to A. Switch sides after a few minutes so the finishing comes from both sides.\n\nVariant: put a defender in front of goal. C reads which option the defender covers and picks one of the others. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass and go – move towards the finishing spot straight after the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: arrive at the far post with the stick on the floor; that is where rebounds end up."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: play it straight back, so C has the ball before the goalkeeper can reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "C: look up before the ball arrives – decide from what the goalkeeper and defender do."
    }
  ],
